  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>This extremely beautiful small cichlid has changed its name quite often. Initially it was introduced to the hobby under the name Pseudocrenilabrus philander dispersus.</p><p>Pseudocrenilabrus: from ancient Greek, means \"false Crenilabrus\" (Crenilabrus is another genus of fish). multicolor: Latin, means \"with many colours\". victoriae: refers to Lake Victoria, where the species occurs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Only bred specimens are traded.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>The natural distribution area of this subspecies is Uganda. The name refers to Lake Victoria, where the species occurs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>The tank should contain parts with fine sand, for here the male builds the nesting pit.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Pseudocrenilabrus are completely undemanding regarding the water chemistry.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Pseudocrenilabrus are completely undemanding regarding food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Plants are destroyed only if they are in the way.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish are agamous maternal mouthbrooders, which means that males and females do not form pairs for a longer period and the female alone takes care of the brood. In contrast to many other species of mouthbrooding cichlids, the female even picks up the free-swimming youngsters in case of potential danger. This unique type of brood care is something every enthusiast should have observed at least once in life.</p><p>The species becomes sexually active at a length of around 5 cm. Keeping and breeding are fairly easy and can be done even by beginners.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pseudocrenilabrus_multicolor_victoriae_en/",
      "html": "<p>Adult size: sexually active at around 5 cm, very old specimens might reach 10 cm; fully grown fish are usually in between, e.g. 7-8 cm.</p>"
    }
  ],
